caption: Prey Countermeasure Array — Super-Memorization
tradition-component: prey-countermeasure-array-super-memorization

The Prey Countermeasure Array is purchased as Super-Memorization. Dreadhound imposes no additional capacity ceiling: the character may buy as much legal Super-Memorization capacity as they can afford.

For a prey-derived negation configuration, each loaded ability must:

be directly useful for detecting, analyzing, tracking, resisting, suppressing, penetrating, escaping, countering, or harming the Current Prey;

be genuinely supported by a governing Talent the Dreadhound possesses at Basic level;

use Only Against Current Prey, -20%;

use the Dreadhound Universal Origin modifiers before Mastery; and

obey all other applicable Psi, campaign, and trait caps.

The repository does not need to contain or resemble the loaded ability. A vampire's blood might support a specialized resistance to its domination, a countermeasure against its supernatural movement, or an attack that exploits a demonstrated vulnerability. What matters is that the build is a legal countermeasure against the Current Prey, not an imitation of the prey.

Before Dreadhound Mastery, loaded negation abilities may use Advanced Psi construction rules. After Dreadhound Mastery, they may use Master Psi construction rules. Changing a configuration requires access to an appropriate physical Prey Repository and follows the normal Super-Memorization reconfiguration procedure.
